# Process memory (ESP32-S3)

## Two different scarcities

| What | Where | Typical failure |
|---|---|---|
| App heap / AXE code+data | PSRAM (arenas, heaps) | `ENOMEM` on load / alloc |
| FreeRTOS task stack | Internal SRAM first | `no memory for a N byte task stack` |

Megabytes free in PSRAM do **not** mean a 16 KB task stack will succeed.

## Stacks

- Create via `ag_proc_task_create`: internal SRAM, then PSRAM fallback (`CONFIG_FREERTOS_TASK_CREATE_ALLOW_EXT_MEM`).
- Uses IDF `prvTaskCreateDynamicPinnedToCoreWithCaps` so ordinary `vTaskDelete` still works.
- PSRAM stack caveat: must not run while flash cache is disabled (keep flash erase/write off app tasks).
- Prefer smaller stacks where safe (FM ~8 KB); AMP default remains ~16 KB.

## Heaps (keep both FM + AMP resident)

- FM builtin heap ~256 KB (not 1 MB default).
- AMP AXE heap ~512 KB when packing both slots.
- Shrink heaps before blaming the code arena.

## Diagnosis

- Log `proc`: stack failures vs load failures.
- Shell `mem` / caps: internal largest block vs PSRAM free.
